---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "Node2Shell / HTTP2Shell is a
  critical vulnerability (CVE-2026-111497)".

  CVE-2026-111497 is an out-of-bounds write in the Brotli decoder bundled with
  Node.js and Bun, reachable when an application decodes attacker-controlled
  Brotli (Content-Encoding br) data. Successful exploitation can turn the
  Node.js process into a foothold for an interactive shell, malware download,
  cryptomining or secret theft. This chain detects a Node.js process spawning
  a shell followed by a remote payload download on the same host.

  The rule chains 2 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 10min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule jhP5r9lpFLqg.
let $stages = {
  seq0: [
    "0ba6868a-e337-49ec-8aa5-da4f19a21e3e", // Possible CVE-2026-111497 (HTTP2Shell / Node2Shell) Exploitation Attempt - Brotli Decoder Native Crash (via syslog)
  ],
  seq1: [
    "67c6a54d-1660-435f-8ff3-bcdfb27af18f", // Suspicious Shell via Web Server [Linux] (via process_creation)
    "e24cf77d-ff3b-492c-9942-0507b45f7ffb", // Suspicious NodeJS Child Processes [Linux] (via cmdline)
    "878fb007-972d-46a7-8ce3-d050642cf7d0", // Suspicious NodeJS Child Processes [Windows] (via cmdline)
  ],
}
sigma rules=[...$stages.seq0, ...$stages.seq1].map(uid => socprime::$rules[uid])
socprime::hos::chain uid="bf5678b6-74a3-428c-8c23-623fc4f03214",
  name="Node2Shell / HTTP2Shell is a critical vulnerability (CVE-2026-111497)",
  level="high",
  tags=[
    "attack.execution",
    "attack.t1059",
    "attack.command_and_control",
    "attack.t1105",
  ],
  stages=$stages,
  timeframe=$timeframe,
  threshold=$threshold,
  tolerance=$tolerance
